      "body": "@grubernaut It looks like the current way to use `aws_iam_policy_attachment` is to attach every resource that wants to use the policy, but isn't it supposed to be the other way around? For resources like `aws_iam_policy`, I believe what most people would do is to create the policy in a central place, and reference this policy when creating role/group in another terraform configuration. I feel like `aws_iam_policy_attachment` should be declared the same way as `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment` with the only difference that this time the policy attached is a managed policy instead of an inline policy.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
