      "created_at": "2017-06-02T23:02:18Z",
      "updated_at": "2017-06-02T23:02:18Z",
      "body": "Hello! \r\n\r\nCan someone please provide for us a complete reproduction configuration (ideally using modules and no secret things exposed). I'd like to take a better look at what's happening here and hopefully provide additional guidance. \r\n\r\n`aws_iam_policy_attachment` is specifically and intentionally  designed to behave the way it is here. I can see how it may be confusing at first though. It is designed to explicitly control who/what/where a role is attached. It's mission statement could be summed up as \"I have a policy, I want it to be attached to these things, and only these things.\" Having two `aws_iam_policy_attachment` with this mission statement for the same policy naturally conflict. \r\n\r\nFrom reading above it doesn't sound like that's your intent. If I understand, you want to construct modules to accept a policy as input and attach it to a variable amount of things. For that you need to use `aws_iam_role_policy_attachment`. \r\n\r\nA full example that I can look at and apply ourselves would better help us get on the same page and hopefully provide direction forward. \r\n\r\nThanks!",
      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "pin": null,
